5577,"Misfire Instructions.  A misfire occurs if a persistent trigger ""misses"" its firing time because of the scheduler being shutdown, or because there are no available threads for executing the job.  Different trigger types have different misfire instructions available to them.  When the scheduler starts, it searches for any persistent triggers that have misfired, and then it updates each of them based on the misfire instructions.",0
