5426,"SRUs will be connected to VSCs at the site. The VSC is considered the host to the SRU.
Some SRU Vendors have a central control device that they talk to and it in turn talks to the host Lottery system.
SRUs use the same protocol (subset of SAS) that is used by EGMs for TITO.
It is equipped with a Note Acceptor that can accept the input of bills and vouchers, much like an EGM, 
It is equipped with 

SRUs will attempt to keep an SSL socket open to the host at all times.  If the connection is lost, the SRU should not accept tickets for validation.  To avoid flooding the host with SSL establishments, the SRU should not try to re-establish a host connection more than once every 20 seconds.
Once an SSL connection is established, the SRU must ""register"" with the host by sending a ""ping"" message. The SRU must successfully send a ping and receive a response before ticket validations will be processed.
When idle, the SRU should send the ping message once per minute to ""heartbeat"" the connection, and the host will respond. Ths SRU uses this reponse to determine if the host is still alive and to set its clock.  The host will use this heartbeat to determine if the SRU is still alive.

Validating Tickets:
When a ticket is inserted into the SRU, it will:
- Move the ticket to escrow
- Start a transaction timer
- Notify the host that a ticket has been inserted with ""Ticket Inserted"" message

The host will send a query for the ticket information using the ""Ticket Validaton Data request"" message

The SRU will respond to this request with a ""Ticket Validation Data Response"" messag, which includes the 18 digit barcode.

The host will;
- Record the validation attempt
- Mark the ticket as pending, if found
- Either accept or reject the validation with the following results
   - Valid CashableTicket
   - Valid cashable promotional ticket
   - host unable to validate ticket (reason unknown)
   - invalid barcode
   - ticket not found
   - ticket is already pending, try later
   - ticket is already redeemed
   - ticket expired
   - ticket exceeds auto-redemption limit
- Return the ticket amount in cents

If rejected, the SRU will return the ticket to the customer, anc confirm the rejection to the host 
- this leaves the ticket in pending state, which will force the casino to handpay the ticket.

If accepted, the SRU will attempt to pay the customer.
- the ticket is stacked in the bill acceptor box
  - if the ticket cannot be stacked for the for some reason the customer cannot be paid
    the transaction is cancelled, the SRU sends ""Redeem Ticket response"" shown below
- the SRU will notify the host and the amount to be paid to the customer will be set

The Host will mark the ticket as paid and sent ""Ticket Redeemed response"" message to the SRU.

The SRU is now responsible for paying the cusomter by any means necessary. 
   This can be bills and coins are dispensed, but could be acheived by printing a receipt
    which could be redeemed at the cash office window of the casino (in the case when the bill 
    dispensor jams)
   This could also be caused by the SRU locking up & waiting for an attendant.
    - cash ticket not redeemed
    - promotional ticket redeemed
    - rejected by host
    - validaton number does not match
    - invalid amount
    - exceeds cash on hand
    - not an even multiple of available denomination
    - machine unable to process redemption at this time
    - ticket rejected due to timeout
    - ticket rejected due to comm down
    - ticket rejected, SRU dsabled
